                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "It feels strange playing this game, it has decent bones and the main mechanics are fun and reasonably well done, but everything else around it feels like a game demo.\r\n\r\nThe \"combat\", if we can call it that is bizarre and barely explained, I still don't really know how it works. You stand around an enemy and eventually their clickable spots open up so you approach and spam E and they just die immediately.\r\n\r\nYou would think the controls would be a top priority for the game in the movement genre, but the mouse sensitivity slider seems to do nothing at all and to slow the camera down from the ludicrous default settings I had to go into my mouse firmware and lower the DPI. Even the mouse cursor settings in windows did nothing.\r\n\r\nThe upgrade system is extremely boring (joy, +10% health and -10% damage taken and +10% stamina) and doesn't add anything interesting to the game. You would think it would make collecting the in-game \"coins\" meaningful but you very very quickly collect so many that you buy out everything possible in the game with them so there's not even any incentive to pick them up anymore.\r\n\r\nA lot of the stuff in the game seems incomplete, like they ran out of money or willpower to keep making the game. The achievements are really strange - there is no achievement for finishing the game! Nor there is one for collecting basically any of the collectibles around (there are some that you will easily get halfway through the game because they require so very little to complete).\r\n\r\nAlso this one's on me but I spent an embarassingly long amount of time looking for the next traversal upgrade, not realising that the objective marker on screen always leads you directly to one. I mean, all the secondary zones are fully open and you can explore them before you obtain the required abilities to progress, so I just ran around in them, trying to find out how to interact with stuff in there for like an hour.\r\n\r\nSo why is this a positive review? Because running around and doing parkour stuff is fun. It even has a bunch of standalone challenges and I enjoyed figuring out ways to get gold medals on them.",
